mode cli

// The non-zero half of the value-returning-main contract: `return 7`
// must become process exit status 7 on BOTH backends -- the compiled
// program's `int main` always did, the interpreter used to discard the
// value and exit 0 (behind the panic test/main_return.til pins). Run
// by two expected-exit=7 singles, one interpreted and one compiled.
// The argument count proves argv parsing and the return context
// coexist -- main's scope is built by hand from argv.
main := proc(args: ..Str) returns I64 {
    println(format("args=", args.len().to_str()))
    return 7
}
